    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The Dockerfile only COPYs environment/assets/ (the screenshot) into /app/.harbor_assets/; it explicitly comments that tests/ and solution/ are intentionally not copied into the image, and no other COPY/ADD instructions reference those directories."
  },
  "test_deps_in_image": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The Dockerfile explicitly avoids installing pytest/pytest-asyncio, noting they are test-only and installed at verify time; tests/test.sh installs them there with pinned versions right before running the suite."
  },
  "hardcoded_solution": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "solution/solve.sh applies solution/fix.patch, which is the actual code change to src/textual/widgets/_key_panel.py's render_description function (guarding the separator-space append behind 'if binding.description'). This is the real fix logic, not a hardcoded print/echo of a test-expected value, consistent with the standard oracle-patch pattern for code-repair tasks."
  },
  "file_reference_mentioned": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "This task requires a source-code fix to an existing repository file, not the creation of a new output artifact (e.g., output.csv) that tests check for by name, so there is no output filename that instruction.md would need to reference."
  }
}

